# Line endings are part of this repository's contents, not a local preference.
#
# Git for Windows installs with `core.autocrlf=true`, so a clone on Windows
# rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. For source that is cosmetic.
# For `test/` it is not: those fixtures are the DESKTOP app's own output —
# a schema dump, parity vectors, a key recovery package — and the tests
# compare against them as bytes. A checkout that rewrites them is no longer
# testing the port, which is the one thing those files exist to do.
#
# It had already broken one: `desktop_schema.sql` arrived with `;\r\n` line
# endings, `schema_parity_test.dart` splits the dump on `;\n`, and the split
# stopped happening — the whole dump collapsed into a single statement and
# the schema comparison with it. LF everywhere, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Bytes are the content here; never normalise them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.archlence-backup binary
